      "Process_Info": {
        "Process_Category": "LB-PBF + HIP",
        "Process_Text": {
          "original": "Fatigue and tensile specimens were produced using LB-PBF (SLM Solutions 250) with Ti-6Al-4V powder. Before using virgin Ti-6Al-4V powder, two drying runs were completed to remove any moisture present. After drying, the powder is sieved (-100µm) resulting in a Dv90 powder size distribution of 65.8 µm and Dv50 of 44.5 µm. Applied process parameters are: 30 µm layer height, 100 W laser power, 425 mm/s scan speed on borders and 375 mm/s scan speed on hatching. Fatigue specimens dimensions conform to subsize specimens in ASTM E466 and tensile specimens conform to subsize specimens specified in ASTM E8. Fatigue specimens were manufactured at six inclination angles from 90° down to 0°. Specimens manufactured at or above 40° did not require supports in the gauge section, only on the lower grip section. Specimens manufactured below 40° required supports for the gauge section. The support method adopted a thin-wall, edge support in contact with the perimeter of the gauge section and column supports separated by 100 µm from the downward-facing surface of the specimen gauge section to avoid mutual contact, thus no machining was required and an as-manufactured surface was achieved. HIP was applied to all fatigue specimens and half of the tensile specimens. HIP conditions were 820 °C, 200 MPa and 2 h hold time in a pure argon atmosphere. All specimens were ultrasonically cleaned using de-ionised water prior to HIP to remove loose powder.",
          "simplified": "Ti-6Al-4V specimens were built by LB-PBF on an SLM Solutions 250 using dried and sieved powder, then HIP treated at 820 °C, 200 MPa for 2 h in pure argon. Powder Dv50 was 44.5 µm and Dv90 was 65.8 µm. LB-PBF parameters were 30 µm layer height, 100 W laser power, 425 mm/s border scan speed, and 375 mm/s hatching scan speed. Inclination angles were 0°, 10°, 30°, 50°, 70°, and 90°. Supports were required in the gauge section below 40° with 100 µm separation from the downward-facing gauge surface."
        },
        "Equipment": "SLM Solutions 250",
